# Release contract for the public boringtun-cli artifacts. See
# docs/BORINGTUN_ARTIFACTS.md, "Publishing a release".
#
# This file is data, not shell: scripts/boringtun-release.sh parses it with the
# same strict KEY=VALUE grammar as pin.env and never sources it. It names one
# exact release of the pin in pin.env and refuses any disagreement with it: the
# release workflow publishes only archives whose bytes, contents and embedded
# binaries match every hash below, from a successful, attested run of the
# BoringTun Artifacts workflow.
#
# BORINGTUN_RELEASE_STATE is `candidate` until the maintainers approve this
# exact release; the workflow never publishes a candidate. A candidate can be
# checked end to end with the workflow's dry-run mode.
#
# BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BUILD counts builds of one source commit: it goes up with
# every change of toolchain, build flags, packaging or notices that changes the
# archive bytes. A published tag is never reused or moved, so once a build is
# public, different bytes need a new build number.
#
# Candidate release: build 1 of the source checkpoint b94943906b11 (tree
# 17458cfeb6fa19d7e37dc66d8a6895b77b57b1a8, upstream tag
# awg3.1-integration-2026-10-06), as BoringTun Artifacts run 37519560954
# (branch codex/boringtun-b949439-candidate, installer workflow commit
# 1d13e6ad51c2698d532ba69b2fb0f3daa8a6e670) built it natively on x86_64 and
# aarch64; the x86_64 build was also reproduced byte for byte on another
# machine. That run's attestations name the branch, not main: they are
# preparation evidence, not publication provenance. Publication still needs a
# BoringTun Artifacts run of main that reproduces these bytes, a BoringTun
# Release dry run of that run, and a separate approval change. The installer
# embeds the published release of the previous pin,
# boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gae2ab44e9a68-b1, until a later, separate adoption change;
# it and boringtun-cli-0.7.1-g71d88784ad29-b1 are untouched. The build number
# starts again at 1 because it counts builds of one source commit.
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_FORMAT=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_STATE=candidate
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_SOURCE_COMMIT=b94943906b11641e274b3c950cc905aaf1631c59
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_VERSION=0.7.1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARTIFACT_FORMAT=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BUILD=1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_TAG=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gb94943906b11-b1
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ASSET_X86_64=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gb94943906b11-linux-x86_64-musl.tar.gz
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARCHIVE_SHA256_X86_64=c6a39a50ccc89f6ac4107d3fe0d530a6f83badc11b405617195e65092e96e7fb
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BINARY_SHA256_X86_64=1210a3c6780948ea07f301c4fa022c0b4ab634da71db0053f65757c8683470d5
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ASSET_AARCH64=boringtun-cli-0.7.1-gb94943906b11-linux-aarch64-musl.tar.gz
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_ARCHIVE_SHA256_AARCH64=cf65174fcb25095a2637544fda860d5d033cd4d271ee7ac40e8f457ece75ecce
BORINGTUN_RELEASE_BINARY_SHA256_AARCH64=c6752410b3994007a9ace5f2d93c30c009b2d7478ebed27b01aacc6168a08629
